# Miles Morales // Ultimate Spider-Man. Turn 1 Bot1 casts Miles (a 1/2) and puts a counter on him and on its Memnite; turn 2 Bot2 casts its
# own Miles, which puts a counter on himself. Turn 3 Bot1 pays {3}{R}{G}{W} (Black Lotus's three, Mox Ruby, Mox Emerald, Mox Pearl) at sorcery
# speed: Miles transforms into Ultimate Spider-Man, a 4/3 first strike, haste legend, and keeps his counter, so 5/4. Camouflage ({2}, Mox Jet
# and Mox Sapphire): a second counter, 6/5; until end of turn he is colorless and has hexproof - Bot2's Lightning Bolt, which could target
# anything, may not target him (the refusal). Then Bot1 attacks with him alone: "Whenever you attack" doubles the counters on each Spider
# and legendary creature Bot1 controls - his 2 become 4, so he is an 8/7 and Bot2 takes 8 - and only those: Bot1's Memnite (not a Spider, not
# legendary) keeps its 1 counter, a 2/2, and Bot2's legendary Miles Morales, not Bot1's, keeps his 1, a 2/3.

[Bot1 Deck]
Miles Morales
Mox Emerald
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Black Lotus
Memnite
Mox Sapphire
Forest x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Mox Ruby x2
Miles Morales
Lightning Bolt
Forest x14

